sledgehammer games co-founder Glenn  Schofield is talking at the studio's  latest project the 2014 edition of call  of duty saying that it is both ambitious  and creative I'm mark Walton and welcome  to another gamespot news update speaking  at a game developers conference  presentation in San Francisco scholfield  said this year's call of duty will be  the most ambitious most creative game  we've ever made referring to his  development career alongside other  sledgehammer games co-founder Michael  condrey scholfield and Condrey have  worked together for many years now and  are perhaps best known for helping  create the Dead Space franchise that  visceral games for Electronic Arts  Activision hired Schofield an Condrey in  2009 to lead sledgehammer games the  studio's first project was called a duty  modern warfare 3 the [ __ ] co-developed  with Infinity Ward sledgehammer games  now has around 200 people on staff which  makes the studio one of the biggest in  Northern California Schofield said the  call of duty series is now on a  three-year three studio development  cycle previously the franchise was  developed on a two year interval with  Infinity Ward launching games during  odd-numbered years and Trey off  releasing titles during even-numbered  years now sledgehammer games is in the  mix as well as supporting Studios raven  software and neversoft entertainment  Activision maintains that this move will  allow developers to have extra time to  not only create new features to help  push the brand forward but also so they  can spend more time polishing each game  installment in the call of duty  franchise will still be released on a  yearly basis so what do you think what  will sledgehammer games bring to the  call of duty franchise let us know in  the comments below and keep it gamespot  for all your video game news
 

